        <mxCell id="note" value="Matches the database after all 41 migrations (latest: 2026_09_28_000002, add_downpayment_to_reservations). Framework infrastructure tables (migrations, sessions, password_reset_tokens, cache, cache_locks, jobs, job_batches, failed_jobs) and the single-row reservation_locks table (used only to serialize booking writes) are intentionally omitted from the business ERD." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#FFFDE7;strokeColor=#C9A227;dashed=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=6.35;fontColor=#374151;spacing=4.62;strokeWidth=0.58;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="329.83" y="1019.59" width="167.34" height="76.17" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="settings-note" value="&lt;b&gt;Why SYSTEM_SETTINGS has no relationship line&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;It is a key–value table (key, value). It has no foreign key, and no table has a foreign key to it, so there is no relationship to draw. The app reads each setting by its key instead:&lt;br&gt;• &lt;i&gt;gcash_qr_path&lt;/i&gt;: GCash QR shown when paying for orders and reservations&lt;br&gt;• &lt;i&gt;reservation_table_types&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;reservation_exclusive_fee&lt;/i&gt;: reservation fees&lt;br&gt;• &lt;i&gt;reservation_stay_minutes&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;reservation_turnover_minutes&lt;/i&gt;: booking length and table turnover&lt;br&gt;The gray dotted lines show this use. They are not foreign keys." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#F5F7F8;strokeColor=#455A64;dashed=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=6.35;fontColor=#374151;spacing=4.62;strokeWidth=0.58;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="606.81" y="937.65" width="173.11" height="114.25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
